recreation
Step 1: JWT Authentication Bypass
Target Endpoints: /api/admin/logs and /api/admin/orders (initially returned 403 Forbidden).

Vulnerability: The application improperly validated the JSON Web Token (JWT) signature.
Exploitation:

Captured a valid session token with the payload {"userId": 6, "admin": false}.
Modified the header to {"alg": "none", "typ": "JWT"}.
Changed the payload to {"admin": true}.
Removed the signature component .
Sent the modified token, bypassing authentication and gaining full access to the admin endpoints.

Step 2: Information Disclosure via Log Files
Accessed /api/admin/logs using the bypassed JWT token.
Downloaded the available log files, which contained plaintext credentials for the FTP (File Transfer Protocol) server.

Step 3: Lateral Movement (FTP to SSH)
Connected to the remote server via FTP using the credentials.
and downloaded a backup .zip archive containing SSH credentials.
Authenticated to the target machine via SSH as the intern user.


Step 4: Privilege Escalation
Vulnerability: Weak credential management / Password reuse.
Exploitation: Executed su - to switch to the root user and supplied the intern account password. The system accepted the reused password, granting a root shell.
